WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:02.980
- You did something that I
like vowed to never do again

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.023
because this is a very hard thing to do.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:09.570
I've sang at a few funerals
in my life and it's just

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:12.110
the hardest scenario ever.
- Yeah.

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:14.450
- If you know them or if you
don't, it doesn't matter.

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:16.630
Because you're seeing other
peoples pain regardless,

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:18.530
and it's just painful.
- Yeah.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:21.170
- But you actually performed
at George Floyd's funeral.

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:23.420
So how did you get involved?
- Yeah.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.180
I believe the family reached out.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.240
I got the information from my manager,

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.890
so I didn't speak directly to the family.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:32.410
But, I believe they reached
out and asked if I would sing

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:35.140
and I mean of course I said yeah.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:37.070
So we got down there.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.490
I tried to sit, a little
further back you know,

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:44.210
'cause I didn't want the
moment to be about me at all.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.043
- Yeah.
- You know what I mean,

00:00:45.043 --> 00:00:46.460
like I didn't want to
do the celebrity thing,

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:47.410
I didn't want that.

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:49.000
But when they saw me they pulled me up

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.210
to a closer pew and I'm
like "all right, cool."

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:54.860
So, I'm sitting there
and, I get up on stage,

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:56.687
and the second I got up
there, I look in the audience

00:00:56.687 --> 00:00:58.850
and his daughter's sitting
right in front of me.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:02.440
And then all I could see in
that moment was my daughter.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:03.273
And--

00:01:04.904 --> 00:01:05.737
I broke.

00:01:05.737 --> 00:01:06.950
I couldn't, I--
- It's the hardest

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:08.250
thing to do.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.680
It's sing at some, yeah--
- Yeah I couldn't get

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:12.010
my words together or what I wanted to say,

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:14.080
that came out wrong,
some people misunderstood

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:15.501
what I meant by that.

00:01:15.501 --> 00:01:16.870
Whatever--
- I know that's

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:18.670
kinda the rough thing too is I feel like,

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:22.230
I heard there was a bit of
blow back from the funeral.

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:23.310
Did that hit you hard?

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:26.822
Like to where you were like
"wait, that was totally mis--

00:01:26.822 --> 00:01:27.940
"that was twisted."

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:29.542
- You know what, initially.

00:01:29.542 --> 00:01:31.160
I won't lie, initially it did.

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:32.980
'Cause I'll be honest,

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:34.510
my manager called me and told me

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:37.450
about what was being said or whatever

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:39.850
and I instantly got upset like "what?"

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:42.050
Like how could anybody really think

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:44.400
that I would stand up
at this mans funeral,

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.100
in front of this mans family,

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:49.630
and mean anything
negative or wrong about--

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:52.170
Like how could anybody make that mistake?

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.003
Right?
- Yeah.

00:01:53.003 --> 00:01:55.097
- So, I got upset and my response was

00:01:55.097 --> 00:01:55.930
"you know what?

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:57.800
"Intelligent people knew what I meant."

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:58.633
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:58.633 --> 00:02:00.203
- And anybody ignorant,
I ain't worried about it.

00:02:00.203 --> 00:02:01.990
But then my manager had to catch me,

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:04.877
he's like "no, that's not what this is.

00:02:04.877 --> 00:02:08.977
"This moment is really really
really important, okay?

00:02:08.977 --> 00:02:10.727
"The least you could do
is take a few minutes

00:02:10.727 --> 00:02:12.557
"to make sure that people understand

00:02:12.557 --> 00:02:14.277
"what it is you're saying, okay?

00:02:14.277 --> 00:02:15.887
"Because ignorance is division.

00:02:15.887 --> 00:02:17.367
"And we don't need division
right now all right?

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:19.537
"We need to do this right now.
- Wow.

00:02:19.537 --> 00:02:20.567
- "So take a second.

00:02:20.567 --> 00:02:22.117
"Explain what it is you meant.

00:02:22.117 --> 00:02:25.067
"Not because anyone is
owed an explanation,

00:02:25.067 --> 00:02:27.067
"but because it's the right thing to do,

00:02:27.067 --> 00:02:30.803
"in order for unity to
be part of the narrative.

00:02:30.803 --> 00:02:32.520
"Not division."

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:33.600
- Yeah.
- You know so

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:34.433
I took it upon myself.

00:02:34.433 --> 00:02:36.150
I went into the comments
and I answered some people.

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:39.957
Somebody said "he wasn't
sacrificed, he was murdered."

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:42.610
And I'm like, okay well,

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:44.230
in the realm of a lot of sacrifices

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.310
they kind of involve death.

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:47.280
I mean it's unfortunate.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:50.630
It's unfortunate that
his death was the spark

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:52.810
that caused this energy
that is slowly but surely

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:54.480
creating change for us.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.300
But the truth of the matter is,

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:59.260
this mans life was sacrificed
in order for this to happen.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:00.124
Now I don't think

00:03:00.124 --> 00:03:03.870
that was the reasoning behind
it initially of course.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:06.620
The cops killed him and it was wicked,

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:07.800
it was meant for wicked.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.440
But, we then took something
that was meant for wicked

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:11.880
and turned it into a positive.

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:12.713
- Yeah.

00:03:12.713 --> 00:03:13.713
No, I agree.

